    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281-a1">

                <pb facs="0457" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg415"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 4, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to your letter of.
                    yesterday’s date with respect to the iron-clad steam-rams from Messrs. Laird’s
                    yard at Birkenhead, as well as with reference to previous letters from you on
                    the same subject, I have to inform you that the matter is under the serious and
                    anxious consideration of her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I beg you to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with which I have
                    the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles F. Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
